## 🚀 Live Demo

🌐 **[Open Live Demo](https://anjx24.github.io/errorcalculatorweb/)**

---

## 📖 Overview

This project integrates standard scientific calculations with numerical methods and error analysis techniques commonly used in engineering and computational mathematics.

It provides an intuitive interface for performing complex calculations while helping users understand computational accuracy and numerical algorithms.

---

## ✨ Features

### 🧮 Scientific Calculator

- ➕ Basic arithmetic operations
- 📐 Trigonometric functions (`sin`, `cos`, `tan`)
- 📊 Logarithmic and exponential functions
- √ Square root calculations
- ❗ Factorial calculations
- 🔢 Mathematical constants (`π`, `e`)

Example:

```text
sin(pi/4) + 2 * sqrt(9)
```

---

### 📉 Error Analysis

Supports:

- 📏 Absolute Error
- 📐 Relative Error
- 💯 Percentage Error
- 🔬 Error Propagation Analysis

Formula:

```text
ΔR = √[(∂R/∂x · Δx)² + (∂R/∂y · Δy)²]
```

Applications:

- Experimental measurements
- Numerical accuracy estimation
- Computational error evaluation

---

### 📌 Root Finding Methods

Implemented algorithms:

- 🔹 Bisection Method
- 🔹 Newton-Raphson Method
- 🔹 False Position Method

Example:

```text
Equation:
x² - 2 = 0

Approximate Root:
√2 ≈ 1.4142
```

Newton-Raphson iteration:

```text
x(n+1) = x(n) - f(xn) / f'(xn)
```

